    d.h2("Non-Functional Requirements")
    d.table([["ID", "Requirement", "How it is met / measured"],
             ["NFR1 Performance", "Interactive operations shall respond within a fraction of a second on a laptop", "Median 1.6 ms health, 17.7 ms marketplace, 22.8 ms admin overview, 54.9 ms price forecast, 99.8 ms delivery plan, 173.9 ms upload and grade, 112.9 ms model insights, 325.3 ms login (bcrypt)"],
             ["NFR2 Model quality", "The models shall be measured and the result stated", "Grader 92.3 % and price R2 0.992 on synthetic test sets; real-photo transfer measured at chance (Chapter 8)"],
             ["NFR3 Security", "Passwords hashed, tokens signed, routes role-guarded", "bcrypt, HS256 JWT [23], require_roles on protected routes, tested in test_api.py"],
             ["NFR4 Explainability", "Each prediction shall carry its drivers", "SHAP top-six features on every grade and every forecast"],
             ["NFR5 Reliability", "Invalid input shall not corrupt state", "Type, size and role checks; three known gaps recorded as expected-failure tests"],
             ["NFR6 Usability", "Plain labels, role-specific navigation, responsive layout", "One sidebar per role, charts and badges, toast messages"],
             ["NFR7 Portability", "Runs on Windows with Python 3.11 and Node.js", "Run and measured on Windows 11, Python 3.11.9, Node 24.19.0"],
             ["NFR8 Maintainability", "Configuration outside the code; automated tests", "Settings class (environment-overridable), 39 pytest tests, strict TypeScript"],
             ["NFR9 Honesty", "Limits of the data shall be visible to the user", "Admin 'Model insights' discloses synthetic training data"]],
            "Non-functional requirements", widths=[0.19, 0.31, 0.5], font=9.5)
    d.p("**Assumptions.** The system assumes that a photograph shows one crop on a plain, light background, that region names come from the "
        "fixed list of eight regions, that prices are quoted in rupees per quintal, and that the buyers and distributors who register are "
        "genuine. **Constraints.** The prototype runs as one process with a SQLite file, the models are loaded once per process, and the "
        "synthetic datasets define the prices and grades the models can produce.")


