def sec_roles(d):
    d.h2("User Roles and Constraints")
    d.p("CropSight has four roles. The role is stored on the user record, placed in the signed token, and checked by the "
        "`require_roles` dependency on every protected route and by the `RequireRole` guard in the web app.")
    d.table([["Role", "Can do", "Cannot do"],
             ["Farmer", "Upload and grade crop photos; view own listings; forecast price and plan delivery for own listings; publish a listing; confirm or cancel orders on own listings", "Place orders; start transit; open the admin pages; publish or plan another farmer's listing (404)"],
             ["Buyer", "Browse and filter listed crops; open a listing; place an order; view own orders", "Upload crops; confirm orders; start transit"],
             ["Distributor", "See confirmed orders and own shipments; start transit; open the live sensor stream; mark own shipments delivered", "Upload crops; place orders; confirm or cancel orders"],
             ["Admin", "View platform KPIs and the model-insight cards; may also confirm, cancel or deliver any order", "Cannot be created through sign-up; seeded only"]],
            "User roles and permissions", widths=[0.15, 0.5, 0.35], font=9.5)
    d.paras(
        "**Constraints.** Photographs must be JPEG, PNG or WEBP and at most 8 MB. A listing must be graded before it is priced from its "
        "own grade; the forecast, delivery plan and publication are available only to the owning farmer. An order can be placed only on "
        "a listing whose status is `listed`, and placing it marks the listing `sold`. Transit can be started only from the confirmed "
        "state, and any distributor may start it; the shipment then belongs to that distributor.",
        "**Known gaps.** The prototype does not validate order quantity or price, does not check crop and region names against the "
        "catalogue, lets any signed-in user read any listing, and does not authenticate the WebSocket. These gaps are recorded as "
        "expected-failure tests and discussed in Chapter 7.")
